# ADR-0005: Store thinking patterns instead of quotes

## Decision

I changed the memory from storing quotes to storing thinking patterns.

Each entry stores a thinking pattern, an optional note, and the time it was recorded. The server provides two tools: `record_pattern` and `list_patterns`.

## Why

I wanted the memory to be useful for reflecting on patterns in my own reasoning rather than storing general quotes. The optional note lets me record context about how I recognize a pattern or why it matters.

## Alternative considered

I could have kept the original quote system, but thinking patterns are more relevant to how I would personally use persistent memory.
